      "narrative": "I'm a lighthouse keeper, or at least, I was supposed to be. My time here has been marked by isolation and maintenance duties, the rhythms of which have grown monotonous. I've lost track of the days, but I think it's been months since I've seen another human face.\n\nAs for my current situation, I'm not entirely sure. I must have gotten separated from my team during a storm, or perhaps I was injured and lost consciousness. Whatever the reason, I'm now stuck in this decommissioned station, scavenging for supplies and trying to find a way out.\n\nI've found a kettle, which I've taken and examined, but it's not much use without a stove or water. I've also picked up a coil of rope, which might come in handy if I need to climb out or repair something. But for now, I'm just trying to survive, and figure out how to get back to civilization.",
